The sheet order is: libraries in the order the rule lists them, files by
path inside a library, blocks in source order inside a file. `generate`
keeps its argument order; dune expands each glob sorted by path and keeps
the order of the `deps` entries.

`zlib` is listed before `alib`, so its blocks come first although its
name sorts last. Inside `zlib`, `a.ml`, `b/c.ml` and `d.ml` come in path
order, which is not the order they are created in.

  $ mkdir -p zlib/b alib
  $ cat > zlib/d.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ".z-d{color:red;}"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > zlib/b/c.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ".z-c{color:red;}"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > zlib/a.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ".z-a-2{color:red;}"]
  > [@@@css ".z-a-1{color:red;}"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > alib/a.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css ".a-a{color:red;}"]
  > EOF
  $ cat > dune-project <<EOF
  > (lang dune 3.0)
  > EOF
  $ cat > dune <<EOF
  > (rule
  >  (target styles.css)
  >  (deps
  >   (glob_files_rec zlib/*.ml)
  >   (glob_files_rec alib/*.ml))
  >  (action
  >   (run styled-ppx.generate --output %{target} %{deps})))
  > EOF
  $ dune build --root . ./styles.css 2>&1
  $ cat _build/default/styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .z-a-2{color:red;}
  .z-a-1{color:red;}
  .z-c{color:red;}
  .z-d{color:red;}
  .a-a{color:red;}
